<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seqenenre Tao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seqenenre Tao was a king of the Theban Seventeenth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the 16th century BCE, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> ruled the north from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a>. He began open war against the Hyksos king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apepi">Apepi</a>. His mummy shows fatal head wounds from axes, suggesting he died in battle or was executed. His successors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamose">Kamose</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmose-i">Ahmose I</a> completed the expulsion of the Hyksos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seqenenre-tao.jpg" alt="Seqenenre Tao" width="282" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flinders Petrie (1853-1942) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coffin_Seqenenre_Petrie.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
